From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] include/linux/version_compat_defs: mm_get_unmapped_area() lost its mm_struct* arg on newer kernels

kbase_mm_get_unmapped_area_helper() in version_compat_defs.h calls the
core kernel's mm_get_unmapped_area() with a 6-argument signature
(mm, filp, addr, len, pgoff, flags) when LINUX_VERSION_CODE >=
6.10.0. On Linux v7.2-rc4 (include/linux/sched/mm.h) the core
function's signature has dropped the explicit struct mm_struct *
parameter:

  unsigned long mm_get_unmapped_area(struct file *filp, unsigned long addr,
                                     unsigned long len, unsigned long pgoff,
                                     unsigned long flags);

so the existing >= 6.10.0 branch now fails to build:

  error: passing argument 2 of 'mm_get_unmapped_area' makes integer
  from pointer without a cast
  error: too many arguments to function 'mm_get_unmapped_area';
  expected 5, have 6

Both call sites of kbase_mm_get_unmapped_area_helper() in this driver
(drivers/gpu/arm/midgard/thirdparty/mali_kbase_mmap.c, lines ~185 and
~403) always pass mm = current->mm, matching the new core function's
implicit use of current->mm, so dropping the argument on the new
signature is behavior-preserving here -- there is no call site that
passes a foreign/non-current mm_struct.

Add a new >= 7.0.0 branch that calls the 5-argument form. The existing
6.10.0..6.x branch and the pre-6.10 mm->get_unmapped_area() fallback
are both left unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/include/linux/version_compat_defs.h
+++ b/include/linux/version_compat_defs.h
@@ -642,7 +642,13 @@
 kbase_mm_get_unmapped_area_helper(struct mm_struct *mm, struct file *filp, unsigned long addr,
 				  unsigned long len, unsigned long pgoff, unsigned long flags)
 {
-#if (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 10, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+#if (KERNEL_VERSION(7, 0, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
+	/* mm_get_unmapped_area() dropped its explicit struct mm_struct *
+	 * parameter and now always operates on current->mm. Every caller
+	 * of this helper in this driver already passes current->mm, so
+	 * this is equivalent. */
+	return mm_get_unmapped_area(filp, addr, len, pgoff, flags);
+#elif (KERNEL_VERSION(6, 10, 0) <= LINUX_VERSION_CODE)
 	return mm_get_unmapped_area(mm, filp, addr, len, pgoff, flags);
 #else
 	return mm->get_unmapped_area(filp, addr, len, pgoff, flags);
